  "realisation_finding": "Every probe is a palindrome in COMMANDED vertical velocity, so its commanded lever arm cov(t,I)/var(I) is zero to machine precision. The REALISED current is not symmetric for every shape: the closed loop lags the command, and a lag breaks the palindrome. Multi-cycle bursts keep the property because the lag averages across cycles; single-excursion shapes do not. The realised standard deviation also exceeds the open-loop linear prediction, because holding a commanded velocity against integral action costs more current excursion than the static gain predicts -- which makes the variance condition CONSERVATIVE and is the direction the one false negative lies in.",
