  "what_falsifies_this": "a single FALSE_POSITIVE -- a probe meeting all three necessary conditions that did not resolve delta_r in the plant",
  "what_this_is_not": "No number here measures any real vehicle. The plant shares a linear terminal-voltage assumption with the derivation, so agreement cannot rule out an error common to both; see research/active_evidence/SIMULATOR_VALIDITY_ENVELOPE.md. Nothing here is a safety argument and no novelty is claimed.",
  "why_the_lever_arm_does_not_produce_a_false_positive": "A drift bias is common to the clean and raised runs of the same probe, so it cancels in the GAP this campaign scores. It does NOT cancel when an estimate is compared against an absolute hypothesis interval, which is what csia_active_evidence.updater does. The drift condition is therefore slack for this campaign and load-bearing for that caller, and the correct practice is to compute the statistics from the REALISED current with ExcitationStats.from_measured rather than from the commanded profile."
